[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_045fbde04029bde3\",\"r_eb76eaa6cd7a158a\"],null,null,[[\"rc_a865bb058c2d4f5a\",[\"### SpaceX Valuation Outlook (Year-End 2026)\\n\\nFollowing its landmark mid-2026 public listing—which debuted at $135 per share—and trading around the **$2.0T to $2.2T** market capitalization mark, expert projections for year-end 2026 reflect wide divergence across major institutional desks:\\n\\n| Scenario | Implied Valuation | Average Implied Share Price | Key Proponents / Consensus |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bull Case** | **$3.0T – $4.0T+** | $300 – $400+ | Morgan Stanley (Base $300, Long-term Bull $600+), Raymond James ($800 high target) |\\n| **Consensus / Base Case** | **~$2.2T – $2.5T** | ~$230 – $240 | 33-Analyst Wall Street Consensus ($235.10 average target) |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$1.0T – $1.5T** | $75 – $150 | Morningstar ($154 optimistic cap), Phillip Securities ($75 target) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n1. **Starlink Cash Generation \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Expansion:**  \\n   Starlink remains the primary driver of recurring, high-margin cash flow. Upside targets model continued subscriber acceleration, expansion into maritime and aviation mobility, and commercial rollout of Direct-to-Cell spectrum partnerships.\\n\\n2. **Starship Cadence \\u0026 Reusability Economics:**  \\n   Operational scaling of the fully reusable Starship dramatically lowers launch costs per kilogram. Hitting rapid orbital reflight cadences allows SpaceX to deploy next-generation V3 Starlink satellites and fulfill Artemis moon landing milestones ahead of schedule.\\n\\n3. **Orbital Compute \\u0026 AI Infrastructure Speculation:**  \\n   The most aggressive Wall Street bull cases (e.g., Morgan Stanley's extended targets) factor in emerging optionality around orbital edge-compute nodes, secure low-latency space data networks, and defense surveillance systems.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Downside Risks\\n\\n1. **High Valuation Multiples \\u0026 Execution Friction:**  \\n   At valuations exceeding $2 trillion against mid-twenties billion revenue projections, multiples trade at rich price-to-sales ratios. Any deceleration in Starlink subscriber growth could trigger multiple contraction.\\n\\n2. **Starship Development Capex \\u0026 Cash Burn:**  \\n   Starship development and orbital test scaling require massive ongoing capital expenditures. Regulatory delays (FAA orbital launch licensing), test anomalies, or payload deployment bottlenecks could push profitability timelines further out.\\n\\n3. **Geopolitical \\u0026 Spectrum Regulatory Headwinds:**  \\n   Starlink's international footprint is subject to sovereign regulatory approvals, orbital debris mitigation scrutiny, and optical interference complaints from the astronomical and scientific communities.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sources \\u0026 References\\n* [Finbold: Wall Street Analysts SpaceX Price Target Consensus](https://finbold.com/analysts-set-spacex-target-heres-spcx-price-performance/)\\n* [Quartz: Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley Split on SpaceX Valuation](https://qz.com/goldman-sachs-morgan-stanley-spacex-price-target-070726)\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://www.thinkmarkets.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://www.thinkmarkets.com/en/trading-academy/market-events/spacex-ipo-2026-date-spacex-valuation-and-proxy-share-cfds/\",\"SpaceX Valuation 2026: Latest Figures, IPO Date \\u0026 How to Trade\",null,[]],[\"https://t3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://satnews.com/\\u0026client\\u003